## Original Content
Ukraine marks its Independence Day on Monday as European leaders gathered in Kyiv and announced new military and financial support packages, underscoring continued backing for the country amid the ongoing conflict with Russia.

## Summary
Ukraine marked its Independence Day on Monday with European leaders gathering in Kyiv. They announced new military and financial support packages to bolster Ukraine amid the ongoing conflict with Russia. This underscores continued international backing for the country.

## Key Points
- Ukraine celebrated its Independence Day on Monday.
- European leaders were present in Kyiv for the event.
- New support packages include military and financial aid.
- The action highlights sustained international commitment to Ukraine.
- The support is amid the ongoing conflict with Russia.


